Vim for OpenVMS
===============

This is Vim @VERSION@ (Vi IMproved), built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@ from
the signed upstream release plus the patches in the vms-vim project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-vim

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  Vim is Charityware under the Vim License; see
LICENSE.  The full documentation is inside Vim: type :help, or :help vms for
the notes on OpenVMS.

Files
-----
    VIM$ROOT:[BIN]VIM.EXE, XXD.EXE
    VIM$ROOT:[VIM92...]               the runtime: help, syntax, filetypes,
                                      plugins, colour schemes, the tutor
    VIM$ROOT:[DOC]                    this file, LICENSE
    VIM$ROOT:[000000]VIM$SETUP.COM    defines the commands
    VIM$ROOT:[000000]VIMTUTOR.COM     the tutor
    SYS$STARTUP:VIM$STARTUP.COM       defines VIM$ROOT, VIM and VIMRUNTIME

Setup
-----
The kit installs VIM$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define the logical names at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VIM$STARTUP.COM

Each user then defines the commands (for example in LOGIN.COM):

    $ @VIM$ROOT:[000000]VIM$SETUP.COM

which gives vim, vi, view (read-only), vimdiff, vimtutor and xxd, and
defines TMP as SYS$SCRATCH if it is not defined.

Settings: each user's in SYS$LOGIN:.vimrc (a file made with EDIT is fine);
site-wide ones in VIM$ROOT:[000000]vimrc, which the kit does not ship, so an
upgrade never replaces it.

Use
---
    $ vim LOGIN.COM
    $ view SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM
    $ vimdiff OLD.TXT;1 OLD.TXT;2
    $ pipe directory | vim -
    $ vimtutor

Vim writes a new version of the file, as other VMS editors do; variable-
length, VFC and stream files can be edited (VFC is written back as
variable-length).  :!command runs DCL; CTRL/C interrupts a search, a script
or :sleep.  The screen size follows SET TERMINAL/WIDTH and /PAGE; VT100,
VT200-VT500, DECterm and xterm-style terminals over ssh are supported.

Options on the command line: "-x" is read as -x and "-/x" as -X with either
DCL parse style; with SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED a quoted option keeps
its case ("-R").

Known limits
------------
- Terminal Vim only: no GUI (gvim), no :terminal, no jobs or channels, no
  Perl, Python, Lua or Ruby interfaces.
- Plugins that run Unix commands (curl, git, grep) need those commands.
